`promptVersionBump()` directly calls `updateNvmrc` / `updateEnginesNode` without handling filesystem/JSON errors. Since this check is described as non-blocking, a write failure (permissions, invalid JSON, etc.) would currently throw and abort init. Consider wrapping the update in try/catch and logging a warning so initialization can continue even if the bump can’t be applied.
```suggestion
      try {
        if (type === 'nvmrc') {
          updateNvmrc(filePath, selected);
        } else {
          updateEnginesNode(filePath, selected);
        }
      } catch (error) {
        logger.warn(
          dedent`
            Could not update ${type === 'nvmrc' ? '.nvmrc' : 'package.json engines.node'} at ${filePath}.
            Storybook initialization will continue without applying the Node.js version bump.
            ${error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error)}
          `
        );
```

_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Reject version strings with more than 3 numeric segments.**

Line 82 currently allows values like `22.14.2.1` and truncates silently to `22.14.2`. That can mis-detect declared versions and skip needed prompts.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-  const parts = trimmed.split('.').map(Number);
+  const rawParts = trimmed.split('.');
+  if (rawParts.length > 3) {
+    return undefined;
+  }
+  const parts = rawParts.map(Number);
```
</details>

