_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Do not swallow non-version failures in a broad catch.**

This `catch` also absorbs unexpected errors thrown by `handleUnsupportedNodeRuntime` (e.g., file update failures), replacing actionable diagnostics with generic version messaging.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix (scope the fallback to import/version-check failures only)</summary>

```diff
-} catch {
+} catch (error) {
   try {
     const { MIN_SUPPORTED_NODE_DESCRIPTION } = await import('storybook/internal/common');
     const { logger } = await import('storybook/internal/node-logger');
     logger.error(
       `To run Storybook, you need Node.js version ${MIN_SUPPORTED_NODE_DESCRIPTION}.\n` +
         `You are currently running Node.js ${process.version}.`
     );
   } catch {
     // Back up in case Node version is so old that dynamic imports or the logger fail to run.
     console.error(
       `\nStorybook does not support Node.js ${process.version}. Please upgrade to run Storybook.\n`
     );
+    if (error) {
+      // keep original error path debuggable when fallback logger is unavailable
+    }
   } finally {
     process.exit(1);
   }
 }
```
